speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I move, seconded by the Minister of National Defence (Mr. Benson):
The House shall adjourn at 1 p.m. on Friday, April 14, 1972;
And that the address of the President of the United States of America, Mr. Richard M. Nixon, to be delivered on Friday, April 14, 1972, before the members of the Senate and of the House of Commons, together with all introductory and related speeches, be included in that day's House of Commons debates as an appendix and thus form part of the records of this parliament.
